  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements :</p><p><strong>Statement I :</strong> Electromagnetic waves are not deflected by electric and magnetic field.</p><p><strong>Statement II :</strong> The amplitude of electric field and the magnetic field in electromagnetic waves are&nbsp;related to each other as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Statement I is true but statement II is false",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement I is false but statement II is true",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Statement-I is correct as Electromagnetic waves&nbsp;are neutral.</p><p>Statement-II is wrong as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p>"
  }
